   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve x^2 - xy + y^2 = 12, for which dy/dx = (2x - y)/(x - 2y). At the point P in the first quadrant the tangent line to the curve is vertical. What is the x-coordinate of P?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 4
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A vertical tangent needs the denominator to vanish: x - 2y = 0, so x = 2y.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "y"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Substitute x = 2y into the curve: 4y^2 - 2y^2 + y^2 = 3y^2 = 12, so y = 2 or y = -2.",
         "mathjson": 2
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The first-quadrant candidate is (4, 2). The numerator there is 8 - 2 = 6, which is nonzero, so the tangent at (4, 2) is vertical and the x-coordinate of P is 4.",
         "mathjson": 4
      }
   ],
